WEBVTT

00:00:08.061 --> 00:00:09.469
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:12.531 --> 00:00:14.511
Take your brother outside
as fast as you  can!

00:00:14.653 --> 00:00:15.633
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:17.546 --> 00:00:18.750
Mary! No!

00:00:20.852 --> 00:00:21.873
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:23.241 --> 00:00:24.486
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:28.010
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:28.725 --> 00:00:29.806
I can't do this alone.

00:00:32.413 --> 00:00:33.086
No!

00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:37.025
We got work to do.

00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:40.121
This is dad's single
most valuable possession

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:42.325
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:44.407
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:44.529 --> 00:00:46.856
You know, saving people, hunting things,

00:00:46.931 --> 00:00:47.870
Family business.

00:00:47.911 --> 00:00:49.768
No. I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:49.788 --> 00:00:51.319
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.136
Sam, You know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:00:54.966 --> 00:00:55.946
Yeah. I know.

00:01:05.485 --> 00:01:07.403
Okay, your turn. Truth or dare?

00:01:07.826 --> 00:01:08.479
Truth.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.152
Do you want to make
out with benji swartz?

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:13.091
Dare.

00:01:13.642 --> 00:01:14.806
Okay, lame.

00:01:15.718 --> 00:01:16.901
You have to...

00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:19.759
Say "bloody mary" in the bathroom.

00:01:20.426 --> 00:01:22.345
Is that the best you can come up with?

00:01:22.712 --> 00:01:23.855
Who's bloody mary?

00:01:24.365 --> 00:01:25.692
She's this witch.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.958
I heard she was a lady
killed in a car crash.

00:01:28.447 --> 00:01:29.815
It doesn't matter who she is.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.961
If you say her name three
times in the bathroom mirror,

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:34.899
She appears...

00:01:35.593 --> 00:01:36.900
And scratches your eyes out!

00:01:39.656 --> 00:01:41.432
So why would anyone say it?

00:01:42.126 --> 00:01:43.616
Because it isn't real.

00:01:45.044 --> 00:01:46.371
No turning on the lights.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:47.949
And remember,

00:01:48.112 --> 00:01:48.949
Three times.

00:02:14.765 --> 00:02:15.704
Bloody mary.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:18.785
This is so stupid.

00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:23.729
Bloody mary.

00:02:34.423 --> 00:02:35.444
Bloody mary.

00:02:46.146 --> 00:02:46.799
Scared you.

00:02:46.922 --> 00:02:48.105
You guys are jerks.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.065
Lily?

00:02:49.738 --> 00:02:50.779
You mind keeping it down?

00:02:51.657 --> 00:02:52.657
Sorry, daddy.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.494
Sorry, mr. Shoemaker.

00:03:32.803 --> 00:03:34.191
You so like him!

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:36.899
Hey, geek.

00:03:37.144 --> 00:03:38.491
You guys having fun?

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.103
You're out past curfew.

00:03:40.812 --> 00:03:41.669
Thanks, dad.

00:04:23.611 --> 00:04:24.754
Why Sam?

00:04:26.741 --> 00:04:27.353
No!

00:04:30.735 --> 00:04:32.551
Why Sam? Sam, wake up.

00:04:41.363 --> 00:04:43.261
I take it I was having a nightmare?

00:04:44.098 --> 00:04:45.649
Yeah, another one.

00:04:49.276 --> 00:04:50.746
Hey, at least I got some sleep.

00:04:50.909 --> 00:04:53.175
Hey, you know, sooner or later,
we're gonna talk about this.

00:04:54.134 --> 00:04:54.848
Are we here?

00:04:55.256 --> 00:04:57.726
Yep. Welcome to Toledo, Ohio.

00:05:01.421 --> 00:05:03.523
So, what do you think
really happened to this guy?

00:05:03.557 --> 00:05:05.170
So what we're gonna find out.

00:05:07.721 --> 00:05:08.517
Let's go.

00:05:37.742 --> 00:05:38.253
Hey.

00:05:38.987 --> 00:05:39.600
Hey.

00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:41.763
Can I help you?

00:05:42.416 --> 00:05:44.478
Yeah, we're the... med students.

00:05:44.985 --> 00:05:45.557
Sorry?

00:05:45.924 --> 00:05:46.822
Oh, doctor...

00:05:47.455 --> 00:05:49.067
Fliglavitch didn't tell you?

00:05:49.128 --> 00:05:51.026
We talked to him on the phone.

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:52.394
We're from Ohio state.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.737
He's supposed to show
us the shoemaker corpse.

00:05:54.758 --> 00:05:55.513
It's for our paper.

00:05:55.778 --> 00:05:57.574
Well, I'm sorry, he's at lunch.

00:05:57.738 --> 00:05:58.391
Oh.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:05:59.615
Well, he said, uh

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.064
Oh, well, you know, it doesn't matter.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.533
You don't mind showing
us the body, do you?

00:06:03.574 --> 00:06:04.798
Sorry, I can't.

00:06:05.002 --> 00:06:07.268
Doc will be back in an
hour. You can wait for him,

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:08.023
If you want.

00:06:08.186 --> 00:06:08.941
An hour?

00:06:10.312 --> 00:06:12.046
We got to be heading back to columbus.

00:06:12.108 --> 00:06:12.740
Yeah.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.087
Look man, this paper's half our grade,

00:06:15.128 --> 00:06:16.904
So if you don't mind
helping us out? Look, man

00:06:18.159 --> 00:06:18.914
No.

00:06:21.302 --> 00:06:23.160
I'm gonna hit him in his face, I swear.

00:06:37.052 --> 00:06:38.093
Follow me.

00:06:41.985 --> 00:06:43.522
Dude, I earned that money.

00:06:43.639 --> 00:06:45.169
You won it in a poker game.

00:06:45.394 --> 00:06:46.190
Yeah.

00:06:46.904 --> 00:06:48.802
The newspaper said
his daughter found him.

00:06:49.204 --> 00:06:50.755
She said his eyes were bleeding.

00:06:50.837 --> 00:06:51.898
More than that.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.572
They practically liquefied.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:07:00.385
Any sign of a struggle,
maybe somebody did it to him?

00:07:00.566 --> 00:07:01.239
Nope.

00:07:01.648 --> 00:07:03.342
Besides the daughter, he was all alone.

00:07:04.168 --> 00:07:05.805
What's the official causeof death?

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.963
Doc's not sure. He's
thinking massive stroke,

00:07:08.987 --> 00:07:10.554
Maybe an aneurysm.

00:07:11.232 --> 00:07:12.870
Something burst up in
there, that's for sure.

00:07:13.448 --> 00:07:14.337
What do you mean?

00:07:14.828 --> 00:07:16.606
Intense cerebral bleeding.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.389
This guy had more blooding his
skull than anyone I've ever seen.

00:07:20.325 --> 00:07:21.284
But the eyes?

00:07:21.635 --> 00:07:23.085
What would cause something like that?

00:07:23.283 --> 00:07:24.850
Capillaries can burst.

00:07:24.897 --> 00:07:26.862
See a lot of bloodshot
eyes with stroke victims.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:29.341
Yeah, you ever see exploding eyeballs?

00:07:29.879 --> 00:07:31.260
That's a first for me.

00:07:31.377 --> 00:07:33.037
But, hey, I'm not the doctor.

00:07:34.538 --> 00:07:36.644
Think we could take a
look atthat police report?

00:07:36.761 --> 00:07:38.398
You know, for our paper?

00:07:39.264 --> 00:07:41.603
I'm not really supposed to show you

00:07:45.702 --> 00:07:47.199
Might not be one of ours.

00:07:47.293 --> 00:07:49.257
Might just be some freak medical thing.

00:07:49.749 --> 00:07:51.198
How many times in dad's long

00:07:51.199 --> 00:07:54.333
And varied career has it actually
been a freak medical thing

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.554
And not some sign of an
awful supernatural death?

00:07:57.694 --> 00:07:59.636
Uh, almost never.

00:07:59.823 --> 00:08:00.829
Exactly.

00:08:00.946 --> 00:08:01.811
All right.

00:08:02.115 --> 00:08:03.628
Let's go talk to the daughter.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.414
Feel like we're underdressed.

00:08:32.761 --> 00:08:34.087
You must be Donna,right?

00:08:34.274 --> 00:08:34.883
Yeah.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.859
Hi, uh... We're really sorry.

00:08:39.748 --> 00:08:40.520
Thank you.

00:08:41.035 --> 00:08:42.976
I'm sam.This is dean.

00:08:43.871 --> 00:08:45.134
We worked with your dad.

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:47.262
You did?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:48.830
Yeah.This whole thing

00:08:49.625 --> 00:08:50.795
I mean, a stroke.

00:08:52.381 --> 00:08:54.322
I don't think she really wants
to talk about this right now.

00:08:54.323 --> 00:08:55.609
It's okay, I'm okay.

00:08:57.294 --> 00:08:58.674
Were there ever any symptoms?

00:08:58.791 --> 00:09:00.078
Dizziness, migraines?

00:09:01.154 --> 00:09:02.019
No.

00:09:03.233 --> 00:09:05.175
That's because it wasn't a stroke.

00:09:05.409 --> 00:09:06.415
Lily, don't say that.

00:09:06.672 --> 00:09:07.374
What?

00:09:08.169 --> 00:09:09.666
I'm sorry, she's just upset.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.654
No, it happened because of me.

00:09:11.725 --> 00:09:12.988
Sweetie, it didn't.

00:09:13.069 --> 00:09:13.865
Lily,

00:09:14.866 --> 00:09:16.621
Why would you saysomething like that?

00:09:17.559 --> 00:09:19.173
Right before he died,I said it.

00:09:19.875 --> 00:09:20.694
You said what?

00:09:21.419 --> 00:09:23.922
Bloody Mary, three times
in the bathroom mirror.

00:09:27.353 --> 00:09:29.014
She took his eyes, that's what she does.

00:09:29.084 --> 00:09:31.494
That's not why dad
died.This isn't your fault.

00:09:32.219 --> 00:09:33.739
I think your sister's right,lily.

00:09:34.621 --> 00:09:36.749
There's no way it could
have been Bloody Mary.

00:09:37.896 --> 00:09:40.118
Your dad didn't say it,did he?

00:09:41.849 --> 00:09:43.322
No, I don't think so.

00:10:08.615 --> 00:10:09.972
Sam:The Bloody Mary legend

00:10:11.808 --> 00:10:14.299
Dad ever find any evidence
that it was a real thing?

00:10:15.094 --> 00:10:16.357
Not that I know of.

00:10:21.602 --> 00:10:22.397
I mean,

00:10:22.912 --> 00:10:23.988
Everywhere else,

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.126
All over the country,
kids will play Bloody Mary.

00:10:29.127 --> 00:10:31.373
And as far as we know,
nobody dies from it.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.209
Hey well, maybe everywhere
it's just a story,

00:10:33.232 --> 00:10:34.846
But here it's actually happening.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.530
The place where the legend began?

00:10:37.856 --> 00:10:40.079
But according to the legend,
the person who says...

00:10:43.166 --> 00:10:45.880
The person who says
you know what gets it

00:10:45.903 --> 00:10:46.488
But here...

00:10:46.511 --> 00:10:48.055
Shoemaker gets it instead,yeah.

00:10:48.102 --> 00:10:48.710
Right.

00:10:49.739 --> 00:10:51.540
Never heard anything like that before.

00:10:52.352 --> 00:10:54.832
Still, the guy did die
right in front of the mirror.

00:10:55.031 --> 00:10:57.229
And the daughter's right.
The way the legend goes,

00:10:57.924 --> 00:10:59.772
"You know who" scratches your eyes out.

00:10:59.936 --> 00:11:01.292
It's worth checking into.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:09.479
What are you doingup here?

00:11:10.819 --> 00:11:11.590
We...

00:11:12.175 --> 00:11:13.555
We had to go to the bathroom.

00:11:14.585 --> 00:11:15.520
Who are you?

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:19.076
Like we said downstairs,
we worked with Donna's dad.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:21.953
He was a day trader or
something, he worked by himself.

00:11:22.236 --> 00:11:23.733
No, I know, I meant...

00:11:23.896 --> 00:11:25.955
And those weird questions downstairs,

00:11:26.914 --> 00:11:27.990
What was that?

00:11:30.072 --> 00:11:31.896
So you tell me what's going on

00:11:32.508 --> 00:11:33.654
Or I start screaming.

00:11:33.888 --> 00:11:35.011
All right, all right.

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:39.411
We think something
happened to Donna's dad.

00:11:39.528 --> 00:11:40.604
Yeah, a stroke.

00:11:40.931 --> 00:11:42.756
That's not the sign of a typical stroke.

00:11:45.142 --> 00:11:46.639
We think it might be something else.

00:11:47.364 --> 00:11:48.129
Like what?

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:49.743
Honestly,

00:11:50.936 --> 00:11:51.965
We don't know yet.

00:11:53.088 --> 00:11:55.193
But we don't want it to
happen to anyone else.

00:11:55.661 --> 00:11:56.496
That's the truth.

00:11:57.408 --> 00:11:58.063
So,

00:11:58.601 --> 00:11:59.794
If you're gonna scream,

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:01.736
Go right ahead.

00:12:04.332 --> 00:12:05.331
Who are you, cops?

00:12:07.857 --> 00:12:08.746
Something like that.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:09.869
I'll tell you what.

00:12:10.126 --> 00:12:10.781
Here.

00:12:11.249 --> 00:12:12.477
If you think of anything,

00:12:12.547 --> 00:12:14.489
You or your friends
notice anything strange,

00:12:14.769 --> 00:12:17.062
Out of the ordinary,
just give us a call.

00:12:25.529 --> 00:12:27.627
All right, say Bloody Mary
really is haunting this town.

00:12:27.651 --> 00:12:29.639
There's gonna be some sort of proof

00:12:29.733 --> 00:12:31.136
A local woman who died nasty.

00:12:31.276 --> 00:12:33.171
Yeah, but a legend this
wide spread, it's hard.

00:12:33.194 --> 00:12:35.532
I mean, there's like 50
versions of who she actually is.

00:12:35.533 --> 00:12:36.690
One story says she's a witch,

00:12:36.691 --> 00:12:38.866
Another says she's a mutilated bride.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:39.989
There's a lot more.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:41.720
What are we supposed to be looking for?

00:12:41.854 --> 00:12:43.679
Every version's got thingsin common.

00:12:43.702 --> 00:12:44.918
It's always a woman named Mary,

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:47.035
And she always dies
in front of a mirror.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.251
So we've got to search local newspapers

00:12:49.274 --> 00:12:51.192
Public records as far back as they go,

00:12:51.286 --> 00:12:53.157
See if we can find a
Mary who fits the bill.

00:12:53.789 --> 00:12:54.888
Well, that sounds annoying.

00:12:55.075 --> 00:12:56.689
No, it won't be so bad,

00:12:56.759 --> 00:12:57.718
As long as we...

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:00.556
I take it back.

00:13:01.234 --> 00:13:02.661
This will be very annoying.

00:13:05.702 --> 00:13:08.848
I'm not sure. They were cops
or detectives or something.

00:13:09.129 --> 00:13:11.047
Whoever they were, they were cute.

00:13:11.164 --> 00:13:11.912
Jill.

00:13:12.029 --> 00:13:12.989
You didn't think so?

00:13:13.224 --> 00:13:15.025
Yeah, okay,they were cute. But,

00:13:15.836 --> 00:13:18.760
Still,do you think something
could have happenedto Donna's dad?

00:13:18.894 --> 00:13:20.280
Maybe Lily was right.

00:13:20.882 --> 00:13:22.730
Maybe Bloody Mary got him.

00:13:23.666 --> 00:13:24.665
Very funny.

00:13:25.811 --> 00:13:27.729
Wait, I'm sorry.

00:13:28.454 --> 00:13:30.653
Was that fear I hear in your voice?

00:13:31.261 --> 00:13:32.033
No.

00:13:33.359 --> 00:13:34.178
Charlie...

00:13:34.412 --> 00:13:36.260
I'm walking to the
bathroom mirror right now.

00:13:37.149 --> 00:13:38.295
Jill, quit it.

00:13:41.003 --> 00:13:42.032
Oh, no,

00:13:42.383 --> 00:13:43.670
I can't help myself.

00:13:44.535 --> 00:13:45.822
I'm gonna say it.

00:13:46.898 --> 00:13:47.857
Bloody Mary.

00:13:48.692 --> 00:13:50.072
Bloody Mary.

00:13:51.055 --> 00:13:52.973
Bloody Mary.

00:13:55.352 --> 00:13:56.171
Jill?

00:14:01.107 --> 00:14:01.878
Jill!

00:14:06.422 --> 00:14:08.574
You're such a freak.
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:15:04.175 --> 00:15:05.321
You did it.

00:15:10.257 --> 00:15:11.695
You killed that boy.

00:15:31.741 --> 00:15:32.654
Why Sam?

00:15:37.581 --> 00:15:38.985
Why'd you let me fall asleep?

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:41.207
'Cause I'm an awesome brother.

00:15:43.317 --> 00:15:44.790
So, what did you dream about?

00:15:45.562 --> 00:15:47.387
Lollipops and candy canes.

00:15:49.094 --> 00:15:50.170
Yeah, sure.

00:15:54.605 --> 00:15:55.774
You find anything?

00:15:56.078 --> 00:15:58.464
Oh, besides a whole new
level of frustration?

00:15:58.979 --> 00:16:01.061
No. I've looked at everything.

00:16:03.158 --> 00:16:05.615
A few local women, a
Laura and a Catherine,

00:16:05.638 --> 00:16:07.463
Committed suicide in front of a mirror,

00:16:07.884 --> 00:16:09.935
And a giant mirror fell
on a guy named dave.

00:16:10.029 --> 00:16:10.918
But, uh...

00:16:12.064 --> 00:16:12.836
No Mary.

00:16:17.163 --> 00:16:18.824
Maybe we just haven't found it yet.

00:16:20.087 --> 00:16:22.192
I've also been searching
for strange deaths,

00:16:22.276 --> 00:16:23.843
In the area, you know,

00:16:24.197 --> 00:16:25.858
Eyeball bleeding, that sort of thing.

00:16:25.998 --> 00:16:27.027
There's nothing.

00:16:27.869 --> 00:16:29.834
Whatever's happening here,
maybe it just ain't Mary.

00:16:36.337 --> 00:16:37.039
Hello?

00:16:44.511 --> 00:16:47.295
And they found her
on the bathroom floor.

00:16:48.441 --> 00:16:51.435
And her-Her eyes...

00:16:52.956 --> 00:16:54.430
They were gone.

00:16:55.295 --> 00:16:56.161
I'm sorry.

00:16:58.453 --> 00:16:59.576
And she said it.

00:17:01.447 --> 00:17:02.937
I heard her say it.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.152
But it couldn't be because of that.

00:17:09.534 --> 00:17:10.633
I'm insane, right?

00:17:12.545 --> 00:17:13.644
No, you're not insane.

00:17:14.673 --> 00:17:17.457
God, that makes me feel so much worse.

00:17:18.432 --> 00:17:19.227
Look...

00:17:22.549 --> 00:17:24.245
We think something's happening here,

00:17:25.485 --> 00:17:27.075
Something that can't be explained.

00:17:28.191 --> 00:17:29.244
And we're gonna stop it,

00:17:30.437 --> 00:17:31.513
But we could use your help.

00:17:50.081 --> 00:17:51.578
What did you tell Jill's mom?

00:17:51.625 --> 00:17:54.245
I just said I needed some time alone
with Jill's pictures and things.

00:17:54.278 --> 00:17:54.980
Great.

00:17:55.471 --> 00:17:56.734
I hate lying to her.

00:17:57.389 --> 00:17:58.746
This is for the greater good.

00:17:58.793 --> 00:17:59.775
Hit the lights.

00:18:04.072 --> 00:18:05.499
What are you guys looking for?

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:07.784
We'll let you know
as soon as we find it.

00:18:07.854 --> 00:18:09.164
Hey, night vision.

00:18:11.036 --> 00:18:12.696
Thanks. Perfect.

00:18:15.974 --> 00:18:17.284
Do I look like Paris Hilton?

00:18:28.969 --> 00:18:30.700
So, I don't get it.

00:18:30.724 --> 00:18:33.133
I mean, the first victim
didn't summon Mary,

00:18:33.157 --> 00:18:34.794
And the second victim did.

00:18:35.145 --> 00:18:36.431
How's she choosing them?

00:18:36.969 --> 00:18:37.695
Beats me.

00:18:42.257 --> 00:18:44.245
I want to know why Jill
said it in the first place.

00:18:45.415 --> 00:18:46.444
It's just a joke.

00:18:46.811 --> 00:18:49.688
Somebody's gonna say it again.
It's just a matter of time.

00:19:02.372 --> 00:19:03.051
Hey.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:05.897
There's a black light
in the trunk, right?

00:19:28.591 --> 00:19:30.299
Gary Bryman?

00:19:31.936 --> 00:19:33.163
You know who that is?

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:35.222
No.

00:19:43.021 --> 00:19:46.202
So, Gary Bryman was an 8 year-Old boy.

00:19:47.115 --> 00:19:49.197
Two years ago, he was
killed in a hit and run.

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:52.121
The car was described
as a black toyota camry,

00:19:52.722 --> 00:19:55.178
But nobody got the
plates or saw the driver.

00:19:55.506 --> 00:19:56.348
Oh, my god.

00:19:57.307 --> 00:19:57.915
What?

00:19:58.359 --> 00:19:59.763
Jill drove that car.

00:20:02.975 --> 00:20:04.729
We need to get back to
your friend Donna's house.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:15.311
Linda shoemaker.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.177
Why are you asking me this?

00:20:20.539 --> 00:20:22.567
Look, we're sorry, but it's important.

00:20:23.666 --> 00:20:24.321
Yeah.

00:20:24.622 --> 00:20:25.956
Linda's my mom, okay?

00:20:26.283 --> 00:20:28.178
And she overdosed on sleeping pills.

00:20:28.295 --> 00:20:29.979
It was an accident, and that's it.

00:20:33.311 --> 00:20:34.270
I think you should leave.

00:20:34.293 --> 00:20:36.071
Donna, just listen Get out of my house!

00:20:40.392 --> 00:20:41.304
Oh, my god.

00:20:42.591 --> 00:20:45.222
Do you really think her dad
could have killed her mom?

00:20:46.603 --> 00:20:47.538
Maybe.

00:20:48.151 --> 00:20:49.531
I think I should stick around.

00:20:51.168 --> 00:20:52.805
All right. Whatever you do, don't...

00:20:52.993 --> 00:20:55.308
Believe me, I won't say it.

00:20:59.618 --> 00:21:00.811
Wait, wait, wait.

00:21:01.116 --> 00:21:03.057
You're doing a nationwide search?

00:21:03.197 --> 00:21:03.829
Yep.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:06.675
The NCIC, the FBI database

00:21:06.868 --> 00:21:10.084
Any mary in the country who died in
front of a mirror is good enough for me.

00:21:10.494 --> 00:21:13.464
But if she's haunting the town,
she should have died in the town.

00:21:13.623 --> 00:21:16.547
I'm telling you. There's nothing local. I
check. So, unless you've gota better idea.

00:21:16.659 --> 00:21:19.003
Why Mary's choosing a victim?
It seems like there's a pattern.

00:21:19.043 --> 00:21:20.245
I know I was thinking the same thing.

00:21:20.325 --> 00:21:22.329
With mr. Shoemaker
and Jill's hit and run

00:21:22.349 --> 00:21:23.871
Both had secrets where people died.

00:21:23.931 --> 00:21:24.432
Right.

00:21:24.512 --> 00:21:25.896
There's a lot of folklore about mirrors

00:21:25.897 --> 00:21:27.900
That they reveal or your
lies, or your secrets,

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:30.023
That they're a true
reflection of your soul,

00:21:30.024 --> 00:21:31.466
Which is why it's bad
luck to break them.

00:21:31.546 --> 00:21:32.408
Right. Right.

00:21:33.282 --> 00:21:34.644
Yeah, so maybe if you've got a secret,

00:21:34.664 --> 00:21:36.498
I mean, like a really nasty
one where someone died,

00:21:36.499 --> 00:21:38.903
Then mary sees it and
punishes you for it.

00:21:39.035 --> 00:21:40.736
Whether you summoned her or not.

00:21:41.619 --> 00:21:42.601
Take a look at this.

00:21:55.305 --> 00:21:56.908
Looks like the same handprint.

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:59.073
Her name was Mary Worthington

00:21:59.896 --> 00:22:02.120
An unsolved murder in
Fort Wayne, Indiana.

00:22:04.346 --> 00:22:07.131
I was on the job for 35 years,

00:22:07.371 --> 00:22:08.653
Detective for most of that.

00:22:09.414 --> 00:22:11.778
Now, everybody packs it
in with a few loose ends,

00:22:11.861 --> 00:22:13.784
But the Mary Worthington murder...

00:22:15.647 --> 00:22:17.030
That one still gets me.

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:18.432
What exactly happened?

00:22:19.896 --> 00:22:21.619
You boys said you were reporters.

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:23.542
We know Mary was 19,

00:22:23.685 --> 00:22:24.787
Lived by herself.

00:22:24.927 --> 00:22:26.730
We know she won a few beauty contests,

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:28.252
Dreamt of getting out of Indiana,

00:22:28.773 --> 00:22:29.715
Being an actress.

00:22:30.214 --> 00:22:32.258
And we know, the night of march 29th,

00:22:32.779 --> 00:22:34.161
Someone broke into her apartment

00:22:34.301 --> 00:22:35.143
And murdered her,

00:22:36.064 --> 00:22:37.266
Cut out her eyeswith a knife.

00:22:39.111 --> 00:22:39.872
That's right.

00:22:41.996 --> 00:22:44.240
See, sir, when we ask you what
happened, we want to know what

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:45.401
You think happened.

00:22:48.971 --> 00:22:51.956
Technically, I'm not supposed
to have a copy of this.

00:22:58.106 --> 00:22:58.707
Now,

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:01.371
See that there,

00:23:01.952 --> 00:23:02.794

"T-R-E"?

00:23:03.295 --> 00:23:03.916
Yeah.

00:23:04.647 --> 00:23:07.333
I think Mary was trying to
spell out the name of her killer.

00:23:07.414 --> 00:23:08.395
You know who it was?

00:23:08.816 --> 00:23:09.838
Not for sure.

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:12.722
But there was a local man,

00:23:12.803 --> 00:23:13.684
A surgeon,

00:23:14.247 --> 00:23:15.269
Trevor Sampson.

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:17.833
And I think he cut her up good.

00:23:18.314 --> 00:23:20.372
Now, why would he do
something like that?

00:23:20.913 --> 00:23:23.096
Her diary mentioned
a man she was seeing.

00:23:23.860 --> 00:23:25.723
She called him by his initial, "T."

00:23:26.524 --> 00:23:27.226
Well,

00:23:27.887 --> 00:23:29.590
Her last entry,

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:32.915
She was gonna tell to his
wife about their affair.

00:23:33.137 --> 00:23:35.240
But how do you know it
was Sampson who killed her?

00:23:35.862 --> 00:23:37.164
It's hard to say.

00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:42.735
But the way her eyes were cut
out, it was almost professional.

00:23:43.897 --> 00:23:45.321
But you could never prove it?

00:23:45.442 --> 00:23:45.962
No.

00:23:46.443 --> 00:23:47.265
No prints,

00:23:47.365 --> 00:23:48.547
No witnesses.

00:23:49.388 --> 00:23:50.570
He was meticulous.

00:23:52.333 --> 00:23:53.395
Is he still alive?

00:23:55.236 --> 00:23:55.817
Nope.

00:23:58.642 --> 00:23:59.743
If you ask me,

00:24:00.124 --> 00:24:03.109
Mary spent her last living moments

00:24:03.572 --> 00:24:05.876
Trying to expose this guy's secret.

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:09.222
But she never could.

00:24:11.385 --> 00:24:12.347
Where's she buried?

00:24:13.893 --> 00:24:14.695
She wasn't.

00:24:15.135 --> 00:24:15.937
She was cremated.

00:24:19.342 --> 00:24:22.027
What about that mirror?  It's not
in evidence lockup somewhere, is it?

00:24:23.847 --> 00:24:24.588
No.

00:24:25.890 --> 00:24:28.415
It was returned to Mary's
family a long time ago.

00:24:30.037 --> 00:24:32.121
You have the names of
her family by any chance?

00:24:37.391 --> 00:24:39.356
I mean, you bring these
strangers into my house,

00:24:39.376 --> 00:24:40.919
And they ask me things like that?

00:24:40.959 --> 00:24:42.261
They were only trying to help.

00:24:42.361 --> 00:24:44.425
Please, Donna, you have to believe me.

00:24:44.625 --> 00:24:46.408
What? About bloody mary?

00:24:46.650 --> 00:24:48.774
Please, I know it sounds crazy.

00:24:49.134 --> 00:24:51.057
"Crazy" doesn't even begin to cover it.

00:24:51.278 --> 00:24:53.421
I mean, it's one thing for my
sister to believe this crap.

00:24:53.523 --> 00:24:55.367
She's 12. But you?

00:24:55.889 --> 00:24:56.851
Think about the way

00:24:57.632 --> 00:24:58.553
Your dad died,

00:24:58.994 --> 00:25:01.058
Okay, and the way Jill died.

00:25:02.382 --> 00:25:03.965
Okay, so...

00:25:05.107 --> 00:25:05.667
Bloody Mary.

00:25:05.708 --> 00:25:06.068
No!

00:25:06.108 --> 00:25:08.011
Bloody Mary. Bloody Mary.

00:25:10.978 --> 00:25:12.861
See? Nothing happened.

00:25:13.322 --> 00:25:14.604
Why would you do that?

00:25:15.145 --> 00:25:16.127
Oh, my god,

00:25:16.728 --> 00:25:18.751
There really is
something wrong with you.

00:25:30.627 --> 00:25:33.572
Elements that lose electrons become

00:25:33.712 --> 00:25:35.055
Positive ions,

00:25:35.596 --> 00:25:38.701
Which are smaller than other
atoms of the same element.

00:25:39.222 --> 00:25:41.766
Therefore, the ionic radius

00:25:41.897 --> 00:25:44.201
Is smaller than the atomic radius

00:25:49.435 --> 00:25:50.276
Charlie!

00:25:55.106 --> 00:25:55.868
Charlie!

00:26:00.818 --> 00:26:03.747
Charlie, stop it! What's
wrong? Just calm down!

00:26:06.855 --> 00:26:08.134
Charlie! Aah! Let me go!

00:26:08.264 --> 00:26:09.024
Charlie!

00:26:11.323 --> 00:26:12.065
Oh, really?

00:26:12.529 --> 00:26:14.642
Ah, that's too bad, Mr. Worthington.

00:26:15.208 --> 00:26:16.951
I would have paid a lot for that mirror.

00:26:16.988 --> 00:26:18.231
Okay, well, maybe next time.

00:26:18.453 --> 00:26:19.640
All right, thanks.

00:26:19.788 --> 00:26:20.493
So?

00:26:20.697 --> 00:26:22.551
So, that was Mary's brother.

00:26:22.727 --> 00:26:25.045
The mirror was in the family for years,

00:26:25.101 --> 00:26:26.436
Until he sold it

00:26:26.695 --> 00:26:27.789
One week ago

00:26:28.883 --> 00:26:30.867
To a store called estate antiques,

00:26:31.303 --> 00:26:32.861
A store in Toledo.

00:26:34.715 --> 00:26:36.755
So wherever the mirror
goes, that's where Mary goes?

00:26:37.005 --> 00:26:39.397
Her spirit's definitely
tied up with it somehow.

00:26:39.527 --> 00:26:42.512
Isn't there an old superstition that
says mirrors can capture spirits?

00:26:43.097 --> 00:26:45.285
Yeah, there is. When
someone would die in a house,

00:26:45.322 --> 00:26:47.825
People would cover up the mirrors
so the ghost wouldn't get trapped.

00:26:48.328 --> 00:26:50.561
This Mary dies in front of the
mirror, and it draws in her spirit.

00:26:50.850 --> 00:26:53.835
Yeah, but how could she move
through 100 different mirrors?

00:26:54.484 --> 00:26:56.014
I don't know but if the
mirror is the source,

00:26:56.033 --> 00:26:57.572
I say we find it and smash it.

00:26:58.925 --> 00:27:00.464
Yeah, I don't know. Maybe.

00:27:04.678 --> 00:27:05.327
Hello?

00:27:06.773 --> 00:27:07.496
Charlie?

00:27:26.557 --> 00:27:27.298
Hey.

00:27:28.244 --> 00:27:29.264
Hey. It's okay.

00:27:30.061 --> 00:27:31.767
You can open up your eyes, Charlie.

00:27:31.814 --> 00:27:33.575
It's okay, all right?

00:27:34.929 --> 00:27:35.745
Now, listen.

00:27:36.431 --> 00:27:37.729
You're gonna stay right here

00:27:38.331 --> 00:27:39.129
On this bed.

00:27:39.731 --> 00:27:41.178
You're not gonna look at glass

00:27:41.345 --> 00:27:43.347
Or anything else that
has a reflection, okay?

00:27:44.155 --> 00:27:45.341
As long as you do that

00:27:46.157 --> 00:27:47.585
She cannot get you.

00:27:50.691 --> 00:27:52.471
But I can't keep that up forever.

00:27:55.314 --> 00:27:56.798
I'm gonna die, aren't I?

00:27:58.707 --> 00:27:59.301
No.

00:28:00.895 --> 00:28:01.581
No.

00:28:03.371 --> 00:28:04.548
Not anytime soon.

00:28:06.746 --> 00:28:07.784
All right, Charlie,

00:28:08.470 --> 00:28:09.527
We need to know what happened.

00:28:10.510 --> 00:28:11.826
We were in the bathroom.

00:28:12.077 --> 00:28:12.967
Donna said it.

00:28:13.004 --> 00:28:14.561
That's not what we're talking about.

00:28:18.029 --> 00:28:19.586
Something happened, didn't it,

00:28:21.014 --> 00:28:22.015
In your life.

00:28:23.867 --> 00:28:24.645
A secret...

00:28:25.906 --> 00:28:27.140
Where someone got hurt?

00:28:33.110 --> 00:28:34.436
Can you tell us about it?

00:28:38.553 --> 00:28:39.721
I had this boyfriend.

00:28:42.680 --> 00:28:43.570
I loved him.

00:28:45.387 --> 00:28:47.681
But he kind of scared me, too, you know?

00:28:48.690 --> 00:28:49.560
And...

00:28:49.815 --> 00:28:50.729
One night

00:28:51.281 --> 00:28:52.428
At his house,

00:28:52.746 --> 00:28:53.893
We got in this fight.

00:28:56.293 --> 00:28:57.716
Then I broke up with him,

00:28:58.905 --> 00:29:01.093
And he got upset and he said

00:29:01.369 --> 00:29:03.726
He needed me and he loved me.

00:29:05.224 --> 00:29:06.179
And he said...

00:29:07.220 --> 00:29:10.130
"Charlie, if you walk out that door
right now, I'm gonna kill myself."

00:29:12.997 --> 00:29:14.441
And you know what I said?

00:29:16.061 --> 00:29:17.335
I said, "go ahead."

00:29:20.351 --> 00:29:21.562
And I left.

00:29:24.769 --> 00:29:26.107
How could I say that?

00:29:31.406 --> 00:29:33.254
How could I leave him like that?

00:29:36.340 --> 00:29:37.444
I just...

00:29:38.230 --> 00:29:40.142
I didn't believe him, you know?

00:29:47.043 --> 00:29:48.211
I should have.

00:29:57.336 --> 00:30:00.331
Her boyfriend killing himself,
that's not really Charlie's fault.

00:30:01.244 --> 00:30:02.369
You know as well as I do,

00:30:02.391 --> 00:30:05.131
Spirits don't exactly
see shades of gray,

00:30:05.194 --> 00:30:05.980
Dean.

00:30:06.373 --> 00:30:07.541
Charlie had a secret,

00:30:07.838 --> 00:30:08.815
Someone died.

00:30:09.367 --> 00:30:10.514
That's good enough for Mary.

00:30:11.321 --> 00:30:12.298
I guess.

00:30:12.957 --> 00:30:14.167
You know,I've been thinking,

00:30:15.112 --> 00:30:17.809
It might not be enough
to just smash that mirror.

00:30:18.404 --> 00:30:19.466
Why, what do you mean?

00:30:19.742 --> 00:30:21.059
Mary's hard to pin down, right?

00:30:21.123 --> 00:30:22.822
And she moves around
from mirror to mirror.

00:30:22.843 --> 00:30:25.829
So, who's to say that she's not gonna
just keep hiding in them forever?

00:30:27.252 --> 00:30:28.441
So maybe...

00:30:29.737 --> 00:30:31.245
We should try to pin her down,

00:30:32.356 --> 00:30:34.565
You know, summon her to her mirror

00:30:35.415 --> 00:30:36.604
And then smash it.

00:30:37.241 --> 00:30:38.622
Well, how do you know that's gonna work?

00:30:38.686 --> 00:30:39.471
I don't,

00:30:40.172 --> 00:30:41.383
I'm not for sure.

00:30:43.993 --> 00:30:45.352
Well, who's gonnasummon her?

00:30:47.157 --> 00:30:47.901
I will.

00:30:50.046 --> 00:30:51.299
She'll come after me.

00:30:53.242 --> 00:30:55.111
All right, you know what? That's it.

00:31:05.349 --> 00:31:06.730
This is about Jessica, isn't it?

00:31:10.935 --> 00:31:12.252
You think that's your
dirty little secret,

00:31:12.273 --> 00:31:14.100
That you killed her somehow?

00:31:17.345 --> 00:31:19.511
Sam, this has got to stop, man.

00:31:21.146 --> 00:31:21.953
I mean,

00:31:22.315 --> 00:31:23.674
The nightmares and-And

00:31:23.790 --> 00:31:25.808
Calling her name out in
the middle of the night,

00:31:26.615 --> 00:31:27.974
It's gonna kill you.

00:31:29.291 --> 00:31:30.353
Now, listen to me.

00:31:31.755 --> 00:31:33.241
It wasn't your fault.

00:31:34.715 --> 00:31:37.519
If you want to blame something,
then blame the thing that killed her.

00:31:37.986 --> 00:31:39.473
Or, hell, why don't
you take a swing at me?

00:31:39.515 --> 00:31:42.000
I'm the one that dragged you
away from her the first place.

00:31:42.213 --> 00:31:43.360
I don't blame you.

00:31:43.905 --> 00:31:45.200
You shouldn't blame yourself,

00:31:45.625 --> 00:31:47.260
Because there's
nothingyou could've done.

00:31:47.409 --> 00:31:49.108
I could've warned her. About what?!

00:31:49.899 --> 00:31:51.556
You didn't know what was gonna happen.

00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:54.104
And, besides,

00:31:54.274 --> 00:31:56.366
All of this isn't a secret.
I mean, I know all about it.

00:31:56.377 --> 00:31:57.906
It's not gonna work with Mary anyway.

00:31:58.235 --> 00:31:59.234
No, you don't.

00:32:00.720 --> 00:32:01.294
I don't what?

00:32:01.379 --> 00:32:03.630
You don't know all about it.

00:32:04.352 --> 00:32:05.775
I haven't told you everything.

00:32:07.943 --> 00:32:09.005
What are you talking about?

00:32:09.833 --> 00:32:11.978
It wouldn't really be a
secret if I told you, would it?

00:32:19.207 --> 00:32:19.950
No.

00:32:21.373 --> 00:32:22.414
I don't like it.

00:32:22.435 --> 00:32:23.986
It's not gonna happen. Forget it.

00:32:24.708 --> 00:32:26.917
Dean, that girl back
there is going to die

00:32:27.972 --> 00:32:29.777
Unless we do something about it.

00:32:30.563 --> 00:32:31.349
And you know what?

00:32:31.731 --> 00:32:34.641
Who knows how many more people
are gonna die after that?

00:32:36.107 --> 00:32:37.190
Now, we're doing this.

00:32:40.025 --> 00:32:42.213
You've got to let me do this.

00:33:09.813 --> 00:33:12.043
Well, that's just great.

00:33:21.834 --> 00:33:23.427
All right, let's start looking.

00:34:02.250 --> 00:34:03.822
Maybe they've already sold it.

00:34:09.525 --> 00:34:10.672
I don't think so.

00:34:23.304 --> 00:34:24.303
That's it.

00:34:27.361 --> 00:34:28.572
You sure about this?

00:34:45.467 --> 00:34:46.444
Bloody Mary.

00:34:49.545 --> 00:34:50.607
Bloody Mary.

00:35:02.223 --> 00:35:03.052
Bloody Mary.

00:35:13.360 --> 00:35:15.251
I'll go check that out.
Stay here. Be careful.

00:35:17.618 --> 00:35:19.254
Smash anything that moves.

00:35:30.610 --> 00:35:31.502
Crap.

00:35:50.036 --> 00:35:50.991
Hold on

00:35:51.246 --> 00:35:53.816
Whoa, guys, false alarm.

00:35:54.326 --> 00:35:55.473
I tripped the system.

00:35:55.590 --> 00:35:56.482
Who are you?

00:35:57.161 --> 00:35:58.266
I'm the boss's kid.

00:36:00.007 --> 00:36:01.452
You're Mr. Yamashiro's kid?

00:36:17.116 --> 00:36:18.199
Come on.

00:36:19.324 --> 00:36:20.535
Come into this one.

00:36:44.270 --> 00:36:45.321
It's your fault.

00:36:46.766 --> 00:36:47.849
You killed her.

00:36:51.566 --> 00:36:52.861
You killed Jessica.

00:36:56.492 --> 00:36:58.297
Like I said, I was adopted.

00:36:59.072 --> 00:36:59.858
Yeah.

00:37:02.577 --> 00:37:03.596
You know, I just

00:37:04.287 --> 00:37:06.432
I really don't have
timefor this right now.

00:37:12.485 --> 00:37:13.823
You never told her the truth,

00:37:14.513 --> 00:37:15.724
Who you really were.

00:37:16.467 --> 00:37:18.166
But it's more than that,isn't it?

00:37:19.122 --> 00:37:20.715
Those nightmares you've been having

00:37:21.150 --> 00:37:22.658
Of jessica dying,

00:37:23.104 --> 00:37:24.060
Screaming,

00:37:24.952 --> 00:37:25.823
Burning

00:37:26.524 --> 00:37:28.796
You had them for days before she died.

00:37:29.784 --> 00:37:30.804
Didn't you?!

00:37:33.352 --> 00:37:35.264
You were so desperateto ignore them,

00:37:35.285 --> 00:37:37.006
To believethey were just dreams.

00:37:37.664 --> 00:37:39.140
How could you ignore them like that?

00:37:39.777 --> 00:37:42.283
How could you leave her alone to die?

00:37:45.129 --> 00:37:46.786
You dreamt it would happen!

00:37:53.478 --> 00:37:54.264
Dude.

00:37:54.837 --> 00:37:56.281
Sammy, sammy!

00:37:58.161 --> 00:37:59.053
It's sam.

00:38:00.845 --> 00:38:02.035
God, are you okay?

00:38:02.226 --> 00:38:03.118
Uh, yeah.

00:38:05.157 --> 00:38:06.049
Come on, come on.

00:39:09.127 --> 00:39:11.272
You killed them!

00:39:11.718 --> 00:39:13.418
All those people!

00:39:13.803 --> 00:39:15.991
You killed them!

00:39:44.510 --> 00:39:45.402
Hey, sam?

00:39:46.332 --> 00:39:47.118
Yeah?

00:39:48.530 --> 00:39:51.674
That's got to be like
what, 600 years of bad luck?

00:40:16.039 --> 00:40:17.377
So this is really over?

00:40:19.227 --> 00:40:20.268
Yeah, it's over.

00:40:22.498 --> 00:40:23.348
Thank you.

00:40:35.261 --> 00:40:36.110
Charlie?

00:40:40.144 --> 00:40:41.546
Your boyfriend's death,

00:40:42.799 --> 00:40:44.561
You really should try
to forgive yourself.

00:40:45.326 --> 00:40:46.367
No matter what you did,

00:40:46.834 --> 00:40:48.066
You probably couldn't have stopped it.

00:40:50.561 --> 00:40:52.091
Sometimes bad things just happen.

00:41:03.775 --> 00:41:04.742
That's good advice.

00:41:21.272 --> 00:41:22.101
Hey, sam?

00:41:23.163 --> 00:41:23.800
Yeah?

00:41:24.788 --> 00:41:26.359
Now that this is all over,

00:41:27.336 --> 00:41:29.078
I want you to tell me
what that secret is.

00:41:34.016 --> 00:41:34.950
Look...

00:41:36.469 --> 00:41:37.467
You're my brother.

00:41:38.848 --> 00:41:40.165
And I'd die for you.

00:41:42.830 --> 00:41:44.869
But there are some things
I need to keep to myself.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
